### Expected behaviour

SBIs should handle HTTP POST requests with an empty body and Content-Type: multipart/related gracefully, without crashing.

### Observed Behaviour

SBIs segfault when receiving said request.

### Root cause

The issue exists in file `lib/sbi/message.c`, function `parse_multipart`, line 2825. Since http->content is NULL, dereferencing it with http->content[0] leads to undefined behavior and causes a segmentation fault.
```c
if (http->content[0] == '\r' && http->content[1] == '\n')
```

### Remedation

A potential fix to this issue would be adding these lines of code right above the if statement:
```c
if (!http->content) {
    ogs_error("HTTP body is NULL");
    return OGS_ERROR;
}
```

